  "constraints": [
    "The final report is emitted once as Picked, Possible, Fallback-Possible, or Context.",
    "CMV cross-molecule evidence requires event-aligned candidate-specific current evidence; host risk alone is insufficient. Non-CMV reactivation viruses retain the prior six-test analytical threshold, and a single systemic HSV/VZV signal requires rank one plus host risk.",
    "Aspergillus spp. may enter Possible as species unresolved when event-aligned mycological evidence converges with accepted host risk or exact imaging context; antigen alone never identifies a species.",
    "Klebsiella pneumoniae identity and carbapenem-resistance phenotype are reported separately; missing resistance evidence remains unknown.",
    "Clinical decision fields remain immutable inside the reporting stage.",
    "Route A accepts only a scorer-verified exact-species low-specificity repeat High and creates Possible, never Picked.",
    "Technical branches are analytical reproducibility, not independent biological specimens.",
    "Reads remain per-test evidence and are never summed across DNA, RNA, or technical repeats.",
    "Missing confirmatory evidence is unknown and never negative.",
    "mNGS-only evidence may produce Possible or Fallback-Possible but never strict Picked.",
    "Partial-QC tests may contribute within-test rank to fallback ordering but cannot imitate complete QC.",
    "Family-aware fallback is applied only after the clinical decision tier, compatible-specimen check, QC availability, and within-test rank; it is a tie-breaker and cannot create Picked or override High with Context.",
    "The curated group-label identity exception is limited to exact-mapped respiratory-virus labels from the curated exact-species table.",
    "History evidence consumed upstream cannot be reused as independent organism proof.",
    "Fallback runs only after all ordinary Picked and Possible routes and is mutually exclusive with them.",
    "The policy is answer blind; benchmark answers are used only by a separate post-hoc evaluator."
  ]
